00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,760
So if we actually try to define what graph engineering is, I think a good definition

20
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:37,000
is it's just the practice of designing agent work as an explicit graph.

21
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,760
So where nodes do work and edges effectively route state between them.

22
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:47,280
And I tend to think of it in terms of three different types of graphs.

23
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:52,560
We have our general execution graphs, which you're probably very familiar with.

24
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:58,400
So these are the workflow graphs with routers and agents as actual nodes that happen with

25
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,800
